{"tool_name":"reveal","contents":["biocontainers","oeb","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biocontainers":{"name":"reveal","identifiers":["biotools:reveal","pmid:17518766"],"license":"MIT","summary":"Graph based multi genome aligner","home_url":"https://github.com/jasperlinthorst/reveal","keywords":["Molecular modelling","Structure prediction","Protein structure analysis","Protein binding sites","Sequence Alignment"],"manually_check":true,"total_pulls":0},"biotools":{"id":"reveal","home":"http://www.bioinformatics.cm-uj.krakow.pl/reveal/","summary":"A viewer for automated active-site predictions for polypeptides.","addition_date":"2017-08-03T18:58:40Z","last_update_date":"2018-12-10T12:58:55Z","tool_type":["Desktop application"],"biotools_curie":"biotools:reveal","credit":[{"email":"myroterm@cyf-kr.edu.pl","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Primary contact"],"url":"http://www.bioinformatics.cm-uj.krakow.pl/reveal/authors.html"}],"documentation":[{"type":["General"],"url":"http://www.bioinformatics.cm-uj.krakow.pl/reveal/"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Protein property calculation","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0250"}]}],"name":"Reveal","operating_system":["Linux","Mac","Windows"],"owner":"mbs_import","publication":[{"metadata":{"abstract":"Methods for biological function recognition in silico appeared to be useful also for identifying characteristics of structure-to-function relations. The introduction of a three-dimensional Gauss function was assumed to represent the hydrophobic core in a protein molecule. The discrepancy between idealized \"fuzzy oil-drop\" and the observed one in real proteins appeared to be localized in the ligation site or in the area of biological function related part of protein molecule. The examples of proteins presented in this paper reveal that the structure-function relation can be evaluated and characterized also using the profile of the difference in value between idealized and real 